  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Parameters**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the request. My primary objective is clear: to implement a \"Sophisticated Dark\" design, using the provided HTML as a guide. I\'m carefully noting the constraints, particularly the need to isolate styling and layout patterns, avoiding any content extraction. This initial analysis is crucial for a focused approach.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Style Guide**\n\nI\'ve moved on to a detailed examination of the design\'s HTML, identifying key layout elements and font choices. I\'ve pinpointed absolute positioning for `.cta-fixed`, `.reel-hint`, and `.philosophy-void` alongside the flex-based layout for the header and hero section. The footer\'s grid system, including its four-column structure and defined borders, is also noted.\n\n\n**Refining the Typography**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific typographical details. I\'ve noted the hero name\'s 110px serif font and tagline\'s small, uppercase, letter-spaced style. The pillar numbers, titles, and descriptions all have their own specific fonts and styles, and the CTA button is styled too. I\'ve updated my approach, to default to Tailwind\'s `font-serif`, which includes Georgia.\n\n\n**Reconciling Layout Approaches**\n\nI\'m now grappling with the fundamental difference between the provided design\'s single-screen layout and my app\'s multi-section scrolling. The directive to preserve HTML elements presents a challenge. I need to apply the design\'s styling while accommodating the scrolling structure. I will focus on extracting specific styles (fonts, sizes, colors, etc.) and applying them selectively to existing sections, adapting layout containers as needed, but respecting component integrity. I\'ll start with the `font-serif` to `Georgia`, and Hero Title adjustments.\n\n\n**Implementing the Typographic Changes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the specific font styles. The hero title now defaults to 110px on larger screens, though I\'m considering responsive scaling. The tagline uses `text-[11px]` with `tracking-[0.6em] text-secondary`. I\'m using `grid-cols-4`, adding borders, and adjusting padding for the system grid. The pillar components are being styled, and I\'m updating the CTA button and the Philosophy Void section. I am now applying these rules in `App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Applying the New Style**\n\nI\'ve updated the font to Georgia and retained the original colors. The Hero section\'s typography is adjusted. The System section\'s grid now features a 4-column layout with right borders and tailored padding. I\'m applying the new styles to Master Showreel & Shorts, and Philosophy Void\'s text has been updated to the desired serif style. The Final Outreach section has received similar CTA adjustments. The aesthetic feels delicate, with smaller text, more spacing, and wide letter-spacing.\n\n\n**Implementing Style Rules**\n\nI\'ve implemented the required style edits in `src/index.css`, updating the font family. In `App.tsx`, I\'ve applied `font-serif` to the relevant sections. The hero title now scales to 110px on larger screens, and I\'ve updated the tagline, and CTA button styling. I\'ve adjusted the system grid, and I\'m updating the System section title, preserving existing components.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
