    checkpoint_index: 1
    user_intent: "Portfolio Customization And Content Update\n\nThe user wants to update their portfolio to include their professional title and a detailed description below their name. They also want to remove the \"Master Reel\" section, understand how to embed videos into the short grid, and change the social media link for Twitter to \"X\"."
    session_summary: "This conversation focused on transforming a basic React application into a sophisticated portfolio website for \"THOMAS NGUYEN,\" a high-ticket visual storyteller and performance editor. The core goal was to implement a specific design aesthetic inspired by \"The Strategic Minimalist\" and \"Iman Gadzhi Architecture.\"\n\nHere\'s a breakdown of the work accomplished:\n\n**1. Project Setup & Initial Configuration:**\n    *   The project structure was provided, including `package.json`, `vite.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, and basic React/Vite setup files.\n    *   Dependencies like `@google/genai`, `react`, `react-dom`, `tailwindcss`, and `lucide-react` were noted.\n    *   Environment variables (`GEMINI_API_KEY`, `APP_URL`) were recognized from `.env.example`.\n\n**2. Design Implementation & Refinement:**\n    *   **Core Aesthetic:** The primary design directive was to embody \"The Strategic Minimalist\" with a \"Sophisticated Dark\" theme. This translated to a dark background (`#050505`), primary white text (`#FFFFFF`), secondary muted text (`#A0A0A0`), and subtle dividers/glows.\n    *   **Typography:**\n        *   Initially, `EB Garamond` and `Inter` were used.\n        *   This was later updated to `Georgia` (for serif) and `Inter` (for sans-serif) to precisely match the \"Sophisticated Dark\" theme\'s HTML blueprint.\n    *   **Layout & Spacing:**\n        *   A \"Void\" philosophy with massive padding (`120px+`) was a key requirement, implemented through large `py-32`/`py-48` values and generous margins.\n        *   The \"Strategic Minimalist\" archetype influenced the use of clean lines, ample negative space, and a focus on visual hierarchy.\n    *   **Component Styling & Structure:**\n        *   **Hero Section:** Implemented with large, impactful typography (`clamp(4rem, 15vw, 12rem)` initially, then refined to `text-5xl sm:text-7xl md:text-[110px]`), a tagline, and a primary CTA. A mouse-follow glow effect and cinematic grain overlay were added.\n        *   **\"The System\" Section:** Structured as a 4-column grid with distinct pillars, using hairline borders and specific typography for titles and descriptions.\n        *   **Master Showreel:** Initially included as a placeholder, this section was **removed** per user request.\n        *   **Shorts Grid:** Implemented as a responsive 2x4 grid (or horizontal scroll on mobile). Each item was styled with a grayscale-on-hover effect. A mechanism to insert video URLs (`videoUrl` property in `shortsData`) was added, allowing for either video playback or image placeholders.\n        *   **Philosophy Void:** A centered, large-scale typography section with an italicized statement.\n        *   **Final Outreach:** A minimalist footer/contact hybrid with primary and secondary CTAs.\n    *   **Motion & Interaction:**\n        *   `motion` from `framer-motion` (or similar, inferred from `motion/react`) was used for animations, with a specific emphasis on high-inertia easing (`[0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]`) for page transitions and element entrances.\n        *   Subtle hover effects were added to interactive elements like buttons and shorts grid items.\n\n**3. Content & Feature Modifications:**\n    *   **Role & Description:** Added a \"Video Editor\" title and a detailed description under the main name in the hero section.\n    *   **Master Reel Removal:** The \"Master Showreel\" section was completely removed.\n    *   **Shorts Video Insertion:** Provided explicit instructions and code structure (`videoUrl` property) for how to insert videos into the shorts grid items.\n    *   **Social Link Renaming:** Changed \"Twitter X\" to simply \"X\" in the footer.\n\n**4. Technical Directives:**\n    *   `index.css` was updated to include global styles, font imports, and CSS variables for the design tokens.\n    *   Tailwind CSS was configured and used extensively for styling.\n    *   The `vite.config.ts` was noted for its HMR configuration.\n    *   The `App.tsx` component was refactored to incorporate all the design elements and dynamic content.\n\n**Key Information for Resuming:**\n\n*   **Current State:** The application is a fully styled portfolio website for \"THOMAS NGUYEN\" with the \"Sophisticated Dark\" theme applied. The \"Master Reel\" section is removed, and the \"Shorts Grid\" is prepared for video integration.\n*   **Dependencies:** `react`, `react-dom`, `tailwindcss`, `lucide-react`, `motion/react`.\n*   **Design Tokens:** All color, typography, and spacing decisions are defined in `index.css` and applied via Tailwind classes in `App.tsx`.\n*   **Features:** Hero section, \"The System\" section, \"Shorts Grid\" (with video insertion capability), Philosophy section, and Footer/Contact section are implemented.\n*   **User Preferences:** Strict adherence to minimalist design, specific fonts (`Georgia`, `Inter`), dark theme, and high-inertia animations.\n*   **Next Steps:**\n    *   **Video Integration:** The user needs to provide actual video URLs for the `shortsData` array in `App.tsx` to enable video playback in the shorts grid.\n    *   **Content Refinement:** Review and potentially adjust the text content (taglines, descriptions, CTAs) for accuracy and impact.\n    *   **Further Animations/Interactions:** Explore adding more sophisticated animations or micro-interactions if desired.\n    *   **Responsiveness Testing:** While responsiveness was considered, thorough testing across various devices and screen sizes might be beneficial.\n    *   **SEO Optimization:** Implement meta tags and other SEO best practices.\n\nThis summary provides a comprehensive overview of the project\'s status, design choices, and technical implementation, enabling a seamless continuation of development."
    code_change_summary: "<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>73-86;102-110;117-146;150-183;189-201;205-231</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added job title and description under the main name, removed the Master Reel section, updated the Shorts Grid to include video insertion logic and placeholder images, and renamed \'Twitter X\' to \'X\' in the footer.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>38-50</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added a \'videoUrl\' property to each object in the shortsData array and included a comment explaining how to insert video links.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>117-146</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Removed the Master Reel section.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>163-183</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Modified the Shorts Grid to conditionally render either a video player (if \'videoUrl\' is provided) or a placeholder image. Added comments explaining this logic.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>228-231</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Renamed the \'Twitter X\' link to \'X\' in the footer.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<edited_file>\n\t<target_file>/src/App.tsx</target_file>\n\t<lines_modified>73-86</lines_modified>\n\t<edit_summary>Added a job title (\'Video Editor\') and a detailed description below the main name in the hero section.</edit_summary>\n</edited_file>\n<viewed_file>\n\t<absolute_path>/src/App.tsx</absolute_path>\n\t<lines_viewed>1-239</lines_viewed>\n\t<learnings>This file contains the main structure and content of the portfolio application. It includes state management for mouse position, data for system pillars and shorts, and rendering logic for various sections like the hero, system, shorts grid, philosophy, and footer. Understanding this file is crucial for implementing requested changes to content, structure, and functionality.</learnings>\n</viewed_file>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:shortsData</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The shortsData array holds information for the short-form content grid. It was modified to include a `videoUrl` property for each item, enabling the insertion of video links. A comment was added to guide future video insertions.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:Hero Section</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The hero section\'s heading and subheading were modified to include the user\'s job title and a detailed description, as requested.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:Master Showreel Section</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>This section was identified for removal as per the user\'s request.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:Shorts Grid Section</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The rendering logic within the shorts grid was updated to conditionally display either a video element (if a `videoUrl` is present) or a placeholder image. This addresses the user\'s question about how to insert videos.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>\n<viewed_code_item>\n\t<node_identifier>App.tsx:Footer Social Links</node_identifier>\n\t<learnings>The \'Twitter X\' link was updated to simply \'X\' in the footer navigation, as requested.</learnings>\n</viewed_code_item>"
