    thinking: "**Analyzing the Brief**\n\nI am now focused on the user\'s request to adjust the opacity and color of the description text within the hero section. My understanding is to modify the text \"Professional Video Editor\" to white with higher opacity.\n\n\n**Refining the Text**\n\nI\'m currently working to pinpoint the relevant code within `/src/App.tsx`. I\'ve located the role description and intend to change `text-secondary` to `text-white` for a solid white appearance. Also, I must adjust the tagline\'s letter spacing to normal and make sure it is on a single line.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Tagline**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the tagline. The task at hand involves reducing the character spacing and preventing line breaks, aligning with the user\'s desire for a compact, single-line presentation. I\'ll test `tracking-normal` and `whitespace-nowrap` to meet the need for \"no large tracking, write together on 1 line\".\n\n\n**Implementing the Code**\n\nI\'ve crafted replacement code targeting the text elements. The \'Video Editor\' title will keep the existing style. I\'ve set the description text to \'text-secondary\' for now and am focusing on setting the tagline to \'tracking-[0.6em]\' to keep the existing spacing. The goal is to evaluate if I should adjust it further.\n\n\n**Revising Code Elements**\n\nI\'ve decided to keep `text-secondary uppercase` for the tagline, and am focusing on size and spacing. After considering alternatives, I\'ll go with `text-xs sm:text-sm` for the text size, and `tracking-normal whitespace-nowrap` for the spacing. Now I will evaluate the updated code.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Code**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the code changes within `App.tsx` and have re-evaluated the code to see if the recent edits are appropriate. I\'m checking that the size, spacing, and styling of the tagline are correct and align with the user\'s intent. The evaluation process is ongoing.\n\n\n"
